From 27a2a50efbeb0710b693c06ad92b90460db8d208 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ttabouch12 <ttabouch12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:07:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/21] Input: add STMicroelectronics FingerTip FTS8
 touchscreen driver

Add a minimal driver for the FTS8 generation of ST FingerTip touch
controllers (fts8cd56), as used in the Samsung Galaxy Tab Active2
(SM-T395). The protocol is derived from the GPL vendor driver: system
reset and interrupt control go through the 0xb6 hardware register
window, the number of pending events is read from register 0x0023 and
the events are then fetched with READ_ALL_EVENT (0x86). The touch event
layout matches the FTS4 devices handled by stmfts.c.

The driver supports avdd/vdd supplies, an optional reset GPIO, MT
protocol B with 10 slots, the generic touchscreen properties and simple
sense off/on handling for open/close and system suspend/resume.
Firmware update and the vendor factory/sec_cmd interfaces are not
supported.

Also add the DT binding for "st,fts8cd56" / "st,fts8".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
